# The pipeline rewrites these every 30 minutes on main, and a branch that
# changes the schedule, the schema or the model rewrites them too. Git sees two
# whole-file rewrites and declares a conflict every single time — the same
# conflict, with the same correct answer, over and over.
#
# `merge=hockeydata` hands them to scripts/merge_data.py, which knows which side
# owns what: the pipeline owns played results, the branch owns the schedule and
# the editorial fields. Enable it once per clone:
#
#   git config merge.hockeydata.name "Hockey.AI data merge"
#   git config merge.hockeydata.driver "python3 scripts/merge_data.py --driver %O %A %B %P"
#
# Without that config git falls back to a normal conflict, and
# `python3 scripts/merge_data.py` resolves it in one command after the fact.
public/data/*.json merge=hockeydata
